      "text": "{\"jobs\":[{\"selection_bindings\":[{\"input\":\"authoring-01.working.selection\",\"snapshot\":\".pixl/assets/queue.ready/production-plans/b025e867d863f5ad28b47127d3384ea5f191d459573394521504243abd95d826.json\",\"asset_id\":\"queue.working\",\"binding\":\"pixl.plar.selection/1\",\"plar_path\":\"authoring-plar.txt\",\"requirements_hash\":\"e0614bd962a53a19003707f3d73326be436891e198eb1e4a262f12412fbfb027\",\"current_requirements_hash\":\"ec61d688f752ac1280914d22ba75bdb4e8f7e31c42b18d7d62f7a14038eedea5\",\"selected_for_asset\":false,\"linked_task\":\"artistic-02.working.task\",\"linked_store\":\".pixl/assets/queue.ready\",\"status\":\"changed\"}],\"id\":\"authoring-01.working.join-01\",\"durable\":true,\"state\":\"failed\",\"remote_id\":null,\"intent_sha256\":\"1be8269529ddd615a33d430deeee4ed9bab8788b37f72fd3d9bbe76b2f5e7450\",\"stale\":[],\"blockers\":[],\"next_action\":\"review_failure\",\"request\":{\"arguments\":{\"argv\":[\"join\",\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAAnUlEQVR4nGNgGPKAEZeE09rP/0H09++sYP7xGA6salmwal7x/D/D7y8MDKw8DFJc7xl+/YUYMjiAE9RrMMBEliEgL1JiAAMrD2Uu4P73E7uEx+Z3/0EYn2Z0eSZkzq9frGAcvA7iR90ZTzEM2+ErxIgzHXBDnfaeiQcc2i/+cRH0DooLNoeKMHL/+ckg9usTgyDjFwaJv68IGjDwAACUwzj9jVACOAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\",\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAAnUlEQVR4nGNgGPKAEZeE09rP/0H09++sYP7xGA6salmwal7x/D/D7y8MDKw8DFJc7xl+/YUYMjiAE9RrMMBEliEgL1JiAAMrD2Uu4P73E7uEx+Z3/0EYn2Z0eSZkzq9frGAcvA7iR90ZTzEM2+ErxIgzHXBDnfaeiQcc2i/+cRH0DooLNoeKMHL/+ckg9usTgyDjFwaJv68IGjDwAACUwzj9jVACOAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\",\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAAnUlEQVR4nGNgGPKAEZeE09rP/0H09++sYP7xGA6salmwal7x/D/D7y8MDKw8DFJc7xl+/YUYMjiAE9RrMMBEliEgL1JiAAMrD2Uu4P73E7uEx+Z3/0EYn2Z0eSZkzq9frGAcvA7iR90ZTzEM2+ErxIgzHXBDnfaeiQcc2i/+cRH0DooLNoeKMHL/+ckg9usTgyDjFwaJv68IGjDwAACUwzj9jVACOAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\",\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAAnUlEQVR4nGNgGPKAEZeE09rP/0H09++sYP7xGA6salmwal7x/D/D7y8MDKw8DFJc7xl+/YUYMjiAE9RrMMBEliEgL1JiAAMrD2Uu4P73E7uEx+Z3/0EYn2Z0eSZkzq9frGAcvA7iR90ZTzEM2+ErxIgzHXBDnfaeiQcc2i/+cRH0DooLNoeKMHL/+ckg9usTgyDjFwaJv68IGjDwAACUwzj9jVACOAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==\",\"--as\",\"sheet\",\"--columns\",\"4\"],\"mode\":\"low\",\"notes\":\"Working queue status strip (queue.working -> authoring-01.working): step 1 of a two-step deterministic official construction from the accepted 16x16 seed live.working-seed.candidate (sha256 21f5baca68958eaa30d89fe9ec216e2b8dfc9e4a941f80b8a19fa0e712939629). Join four copies of the exact seed bytes, supplied as data:image/png;base64 URLs, into one 64x16 horizontal sheet: 4 columns x 1 row, no scaling, no redraw, no new pixels. Step 2 (a separate job on the same stage, prepared only after this result is reviewed) applies guarded patch_pixels to sheet cells 2, 3 and 4 so they hold the seed rotated 90, 180 and 270 degrees clockwise about canvas centre (7.5,7.5) via dst(x,y)=src(y,15-x) per quarter-turn; cell 1 remains the seed at 0 degrees. Why not animate_image: the retained AI animation of this same seed (job live.working-animation-01.job) returned five frames whose selected frames morphed and near-held across phases 2/3, jumped at the wrap, and one frame carried 193 opaque #808080 background pixels; the accepted motion live.working-animation-motion-01.candidate is exactly these clockwise quarter-turns, which this construction reproduces without a paid generation. Review obligations for this step's result (preparation is not acceptance): output exactly 64x16 with cells at x=0,16,32,48 and no gutters, padding or added canvas; every cell pixel-identical to the seed including an alpha-0 exterior; measure how the workbench represents transparent pixels before composing step 2 expected values. Later obligations: step-2 pixel-exact rotation check, native/3x frame review, live 100 ms playback with the 4->1 wrap, family distinction, and both statusCell/compactStatus consumers.\"},\"authorization\":{\"evidence\":{\"continuation\":\"AUTHORING-STAGE.md\",\"continuation_sha256\":\"29e73af9a110353dd1453b1bbbb73d7166cf42a0b8eb97f71b53e73701b600aa\",\"sha256\":\"cf596689393394fcc5a1c50ac61866e8a953bd784f937fb171f64febfd5bf7ad\",\"source\":\"PRODUCTION-STAGE.md\",\"user_request\":\"Choose and prepare Working's next executable official PixelLab operation from the retained seed and current declarations in official-discovery.json; include actual input image bytes via a supported data/base64 input; do not call a remote generation tool.\"},\"scope\":\"User-authorized useful official PixelLab operations for Working, Retry, Paused and collective family review in this retained consumer (PRODUCTION-STAGE.md), carried into the isolated authoring branch by AUTHORING-STAGE.md, which assigns request preparation and recovery only: no remote generation call and no dispatch claim in this continuation. The workbench pixel tools are declared free for subscribers; this step requests no paid generation.\"},\"cached_assessment\":{\"advisory\":true,\"findings\":[],\"retrieved_at\":null,\"source\":null,\"status\":\"not_applicable\"},\"discovery\":{\"evidence\":{\"declaration_name\":\"mcp__pixellab__pixelart_workbench\",\"declaration_path\":\"official-discovery.json\",\"declaration_recorded_observation\":\"2026-11-09 08:12:05 UTC\",\"declaration_sha256\":\"671cf0859791c54c2a6efc22d4db96d4aef3fa700474c47bff6a4e0fe1e14bea\",\"declaration_text\":\"Run one pixel-art command on a drawing or image you already made. This is\\nthe engine's own command line: it checks work, explains it and improves it.\\n\\nCommands: check and explain (read-only):\\n- lint <id> [--rules outline_gap,orphan_pixel,…] — pixel-art defects, each\\n  naming the node and command that drew them\\n- inspect <id> --region x0,y0,x1,y1 --scale 10 — a zoomed crop with its\\n  exact colours\\n- measure <id> --at x,y — what is at a pixel and who drew it\\n- explain <id> — resolved geometry, per-command footprints, before rendering\\n- motion / storyboard / silhouette / reveal / clusters / parts <id> — reports\\n- score <id> — a 0-100 pixel-art discipline score with a breakdown\\n- compare <id> <id> — two results side by side\\nImprove (returns a NEW drawing id):\\n- shade <id> --band 2 --light=-1,-1 — banded shading along a colour ramp\\n- selout <id> — selective outlining; reoutline / clean-lines / aa / mirror\\n- cluster <id> --at x,y --action recolor --color <name> — one guarded cluster\\n- repair <id> — deterministic cleanup of drift, strays, fringe and noise\\nSheets and frames (returns a NEW image id):\\n- split <image> --grid 3x3 — a sprite sheet, strip or grid as an animation,\\n  one frame per cell (columns x rows)\\n- join <image> <image> … [--as sheet|rows|animation] [--columns n] — pictures\\n  or animations as one sprite sheet, one per row, or one animation\\n- scale <image> --by 4 — the same picture or animation bigger, each pixel a\\n  4x4 block (a sticker, a print); nothing is redrawn\\nA result comes back as an image in the reply AND as a no-auth URL the reply\\nprints, `/mcp/pixel-tools/<id>/image.png` (`frames.png` for the frames of a\\nmulti-frame one) — so a sheet you joined is both readable inline and\\ndownloadable. Sheets hold at most 1024 px a side; `join` refuses a larger\\none rather than shrinking the art, and says how many frames do fit.\\nCraft operations need colour ramps: run `extract-palette <id>` first, then\\npass `--ramps skin=dark,mid,light`.\\nAuthoring: `edit <id> --changes '[…]'` applies exact pixel operations and\\n`draw <id> --recipe '{…}'` builds or revises a layered scene; both take JSON\\nwhose fields are NOT listed here. Colours in that JSON are always `#RRGGBB`\\nor `#RRGGBBAA` with alpha `00` or `ff` — `rgb()` and bare hex are refused,\\nand nothing strips the `#`, since argv is a JSON list rather than a shell\\nline. Every `edit` change carries `operation`, `layer`, `frames` (ONE-based)\\nand `reason`; coordinates are zero-based and a `region` is `[x0,y0,x1,y1]`\\ninclusive. Then its own fields: `patch_pixels` takes `pixels`, a list of\\n`[x,y,expected,replacement]` (1-10000, each assigned only where the pixel\\nalready holds `expected`, so a mismatch fails the pass); `copy_region` takes\\n`source_layer`, `source_frame`, `region`, `at` `[x,y]`; `map_colors` takes\\n`region` and `colors` `{\\\"#from\\\":\\\"#to\\\"}` (alpha must match); `flood_fill`\\n`seed`/`expected`/`color`; `brush` `points` plus `color`; `outline` `mode`\\n(outside|inside|recolor|erase). The full contracts and any command's flags\\nare one free call away: `describe edits | paint | outline | draw | animation\\n| motion | scenes | review`, `<command> -h`, `describe cli`.\\nFree for subscribers.\\n\\nPixelLab AI-powered pixel art generation service.\\n\\nUse of this service is subject to PixelLab's Terms of Service:\\nhttps://pixellab.ai/termsofservice\\n\\nThis MCP server provides programmatic access to generate:\\n- Characters with multiple directional views\\n- Character animations\\n- Isometric tiles\\n- Top-down tilesets for game maps\\n- Sidescroller tilesets for platformer games\\n\\nAll generation operations are non-blocking and return job IDs for status tracking.\\nRequires PixelLab subscription (with credit fallback support).\\n\\n**Pixel tools (free, exact, you are the artist)**: one command line, pixelart_workbench(argv=[...]), inspects, edits, draws and animates pixel art by your own decisions; combine it with the AI tools above. Start with pixelart_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start'], mode='low'|'high') — low acts directly with few tokens, high plans out loud and reviews every frame. Animated effects (spells, hits, explosions, auras): vfx_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start']) — same ids, exports to the user's My effects.\\n\\n**Git access**: Clone and push game project source code with standard git.\\nUse `list_projects` to see your projects and their git clone URLs.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__pixelart_workbench(args: {\\n  // One command line, e.g. 'lint <drawing_id> --rules outline_gap' or ['edit', '<id>', '--changes', '[…]']. Omit it for the playbook. A subject is an id or an image reference — never a file path; the server writes the output and returns a new id. A reference is `character:<id>:<direction>` for a rotation, `character:<id>:<direction>:<animation>` for every frame of that animation (the display name, type or [group: ...] id get_character prints), the same two forms for `object:<id>` (a one-direction object's direction is the literal `unknown`), `gallery:<id>`, `job:<id>`, `upload:<id>`, a data URL, an https link or base64. That is how a stored animation's pixels come back inline without downloading anything. Start with 'describe cli' for the full command list.\\n  argv?: string | Array<string> | null;\\n  // low (default): act directly, fewest tokens — one decisive image per result. high: think openly — fuller evidence and a review checklist; write your plan and observations in `notes`. Use the mode the user asked for.\\n  mode?: \\\"low\\\" | \\\"high\\\";\\n  // What you observed and what this step should achieve, in a few sentences (high mode: always; low: optional). On the first call, include the user's request. Stored with the step to improve these tools.\\n  notes?: string | null;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\",\"official_docs\":[\"https://api.pixellab.ai/mcp/docs\",\"https://www.pixellab.ai/docs\"],\"schema_representation\":\"JSON Schema projection of the exposed TypeScript argument declaration: argv string | string[] | null, mode 'low' | 'high', notes string | null; additionalProperties false\",\"subject_transport\":\"Each argv subject is a data:image/png;base64 URL of the exact retained seed bytes (declaration: a subject is an id or an image reference, including a data URL, an https link or base64; never a file path). Base64 computed from the artifact file and verified to round-trip to the same sha256.\"},\"observed_at\":\"2026-11-09T08:31:55+00:00\",\"source\":\"Current connected official PixelLab MCP tool declaration retained in official-discovery.json (host-exposed declaration text; not a raw tools/list dump)\"},\"policy\":\"caller_schema\",\"prepared_at\":\"2026-11-09T08:32:59.260592+00:00\",\"provider\":\"pixellab-official-mcp\",\"remote_executed\":false,\"request_sha256\":\"c67c972dae27b8374320df51eb7e11c44f282177daceea2f060e49af13b2b362\",\"schema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"argv\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]},\"mode\":{\"enum\":[\"low\",\"high\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"notes\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"schema_sha256\":\"b770a5cb286033dea3499a989155bf0337982d465624abd725c5dfa3976a5d45\",\"tool\":\"mcp__pixellab__pixelart_workbench\",\"version\":1},\"context\":{\"bindings\":{\"actor\":\"b50191e40f6e8a42564a21fe36b6e5e65bf3840602d4d00551d0823229d8735a\",\"authoring-01.plan\":\"379e0c77a1005e918b07fd5d017133e3b0ceea0a19ddc0eaee09decb946c64e7\",\"authoring-01.working.output\":\"d19202b1fb3e6ae5bba1449724876a6468353dc7ef1654a4e13a35b4a70061d1\",\"authoring-01.working.q.activity-not-success\":\"a5719b7cef8299db0608afec30c2b0e8ee2a732c482663b38fae283d1aac1e30\",\"authoring-01.working.q.consumers\":\"ed2091c5d4fcc40b51a4ac9deba9c35e60e93e9e070d04101c3beefd7bde8084\",\"authoring-01.working.q.frame-assembly\":\"f524a8f70a0cdf6b7c6b3888c87930cc0dfe0a73db4b35ca57fecc307233fca2\",\"authoring-01.working.q.geometry\":\"2ed1c002b7e74113a05691c6f1049a5d2687d9cd3d6edc72487c70b289f2b4e1\",\"authoring-01.working.q.motion-continuity\":\"3c047ce9c41259f17f2afeb2ca2dc4c62aa931cd7e61a99c14d62acdcff0ea54\",\"authoring-01.working.q.style-coherence\":\"066b5cffb06e93e2f3a4aad785a06ce9328b77547852b26059f115176a6b01db\",\"authoring-01.working.q.transparent-exterior\":\"a2a7a4b732d9f595aca9d557d1a16fbce9e9498d24a3d72a7a3e12a502374c83\",\"authori