            "notes": "Working queue status strip (queue.working -> authoring-01.working): step 1 of a two-step deterministic official construction from the accepted 16x16 seed live.working-seed.candidate (sha256 21f5baca68958eaa30d89fe9ec216e2b8dfc9e4a941f80b8a19fa0e712939629). Join four copies of the exact seed bytes, supplied as data:image/png;base64 URLs, into one 64x16 horizontal sheet: 4 columns x 1 row, no scaling, no redraw, no new pixels. Step 2 (a separate job on the same stage, prepared only after this result is reviewed) applies guarded patch_pixels to sheet cells 2, 3 and 4 so they hold the seed rotated 90, 180 and 270 degrees clockwise about canvas centre (7.5,7.5) via dst(x,y)=src(y,15-x) per quarter-turn; cell 1 remains the seed at 0 degrees. Why not animate_image: the retained AI animation of this same seed (job live.working-animation-01.job) returned five frames whose selected frames morphed and near-held across phases 2/3, jumped at the wrap, and one frame carried 193 opaque #808080 background pixels; the accepted motion live.working-animation-motion-01.candidate is exactly these clockwise quarter-turns, which this construction reproduces without a paid generation. Review obligations for this step's result (preparation is not acceptance): output exactly 64x16 with cells at x=0,16,32,48 and no gutters, padding or added canvas; every cell pixel-identical to the seed including an alpha-0 exterior; measure how the workbench represents transparent pixels before composing step 2 expected values. Later obligations: step-2 pixel-exact rotation check, native/3x frame review, live 100 ms playback with the 4->1 wrap, family distinction, and both statusCell/compactStatus consumers."
